            <ArticleTitle>A papular eruption and acute abdominal pain associated with coxsackie A-14 virus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>127-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 14-year-old girl who was admitted to hospital with acute abdominal pain developed an erythematous papular eruption which persisted for 4 weeks. Examination of a stool specimen yielded evidence of a coxsackie A-14 virus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
